Custom Pipes:

Why custom pipes ?
->> To perform any advance transformations on template easily and effectively.
example: sorting, filtering, power, exponent and paginator etc

To create custom pipe:
ng g pipe "pipe-name-here"

->> import pipe, pipeTransform from angular/core
->> The main method for creating a custom pipe is the transform() method and with it we can perform any kind of changes on imput value.

->> | symbol for pipe- it is union type in Angular-typescript.

There are two types of pipes:
1. Pure pipe
2. Impure pipe

1.pure pipe:(default)
->> A pure pipe process input and return values without any side effects.

2. Impure pipe:
->> An impure pipe transform the data even if the input hasn't changed.
->> To set pipe as impure, declare pipe: false inside @pipe decorator